Sounds like a level teleport trap not a regular teleport trap.  Let's
see if I understand how a level teleport trap works: It will move any
number of monsters to other levels but if your character uses it to
move to another level it disappears after one use, much like a
polymorph trap.  I think this behavior was put in to prevent abuses.

> What is the difference between MC and MR? I haven't been able to
> understand from reading about it in "Maniac's Ascension Guide".

In spite of their similar names they are quite different.  MR gives
complete immunity to a list of magical attacks.  Magic missile
is the most obvious one based on the name.  MC gives statistical
chance at immunity to a different list of monster attacks.  Vampire
bites may be the most obvious.

It turns out that it is much easier to observe MR than MC.  If you
get zapped with magic missiles and you're immune your MC gets
pretty obvious.  MC is much harder to observe - Vampires and
other monsters don't seem to be effective with no obvious reason.

Notice that when you take off a cloak it gives a more informative
message than when you take off other armor.  I've never checked
whether taking off any MC!=0 armor does that, but it would be a
very nice feature to implement to make MC more observable.

